# Local development environment for the Go server.
#
#   cp apps/server/.env.example apps/server/.env
#   cd apps/server && set -a && source .env && set +a && go run ./cmd/server
#
# The server reads real environment variables only — there is no dotenv loader
# in the binary — so this file has to be *sourced*, not just present.
#
# Convention: `*.example` is committed, your filled-in copy is git-ignored.
# The compose stacks have their own pair in deploy/compose:
# `.env.dev.example` → `.env` (auto-loaded by compose.dev.yml) and
# `.env.prod.example` → `.env.prod` (passed with --env-file).
# Values here assume the services from deploy/compose/compose.dev.yml, which
# publish their ports to localhost.

PP_ADDR=:8080

# The origin the *browser* uses. In development that is the Vite dev server,
# which proxies /api, /auth and /s/ to :8080, so the post-login redirect to
# "/" lands on the SPA rather than on the bare API port. Register
# http://localhost:5173/auth/callback with the IdP to match.
PP_EXTERNAL_URL=http://localhost:5173

# compose.dev.yml creates user/db "pphub". If 5432 is already taken on your
# host, set PP_POSTGRES_PORT in deploy/compose/.env and use it here too.
PP_DATABASE_URL=postgres://pphub:pphub@localhost:5432/pphub?sslmode=disable

# ── OIDC ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logto Cloud (https://<tenant>.logto.app/oidc), or http://localhost:3001/oidc
# with `--profile idp` (admin console on http://localhost:3002, first visit
# claims the owner account). Register the app as Traditional Web with redirect
# URI http://localhost:5173/auth/callback — PP_EXTERNAL_URL above.
PP_OIDC_ISSUER=https://your-tenant.logto.app/oidc
PP_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=your-app-id
PP_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=your-app-secret
# Only when the issuer differs between the server and the browser.
# PP_OIDC_ISSUER_EXTERNAL=
# Mirror the IdP's phone_number onto profiles by also requesting the `phone`
# scope. Off by default: a provider that has not granted this client the scope
# fails the sign-in instead of omitting the claim. On Logto, a third-party
# application must first list "phone" under its Permissions.
# PP_OIDC_PHONE_SCOPE=1

# ── Logto (required) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logto is the identity provider and the source of truth for who belongs to
# which space; see docs/architecture/logto-org-sync.md. The server refuses to
# start without the endpoint and the M2M credentials.
#
# The endpoint is Logto's base URL, NOT the OIDC issuer: no /oidc suffix.
# The credentials are a machine-to-machine application holding the Logto
# Management API `all` permission.
PP_LOGTO_ENDPOINT=https://your-tenant.logto.app
PP_LOGTO_M2M_CLIENT_ID=
PP_LOGTO_M2M_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Audience of the M2M token. Cloud: https://<tenant-id>.logto.app/api
# Open source: https://default.logto.app/api (the default below).
PP_LOGTO_API_RESOURCE=https://default.logto.app/api
# Signs webhook deliveries to POST {PP_EXTERNAL_URL}/hooks/logto. Unset closes
# that route; changes made in Logto then arrive at the next sign-in or the
# hourly sweep instead of immediately. Subscribe the webhook to
# Organization.Membership.Updated, Organization.Data.Updated,
# Organization.Deleted, User.Data.Updated, User.SuspensionStatus.Updated and
# User.Deleted.
PP_LOGTO_WEBHOOK_KEY=
# The organization role that maps onto a space's Admin group. It must exist in
# your organization template.
PP_LOGTO_ORG_ROLE_ADMIN=admin

# ── OnlyOffice ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Browser-facing: goes into the editor iframe.
PP_ONLYOFFICE_URL=http://localhost:9980
# How OnlyOffice reaches *this* server's WOPI listener (PP_WOPI_ADDR, default
# :8081 — a port of its own, not the public one). It runs in Docker while the
# server runs on your host, so it goes through the `wopi-proxy` service in
# compose.dev.yml, whose name the Document Server's ipfilter allows
# (OnlyOffice 10 refuses host.docker.internal on OrbStack).
PP_WOPI_SERVER_URL=http://wopi-proxy:8081

# ── Publishing (M50) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Empty serves published sites under /a/ on PP_EXTERNAL_URL (sandbox CSP
# only); set to a separate domain routed to this service to isolate them. It
# must then be a different HOST from PP_EXTERNAL_URL (the server refuses to
# start otherwise) — locally, 127.0.0.1 next to localhost is enough: browse
# the app on http://localhost:5173 (or :8080) and set this to
# http://127.0.0.1:8080. Either way, turn on Admin › Settings › Sharing ›
# Publishing.
PP_ARTIFACT_URL=
# Ceiling on one publication's snapshot, all files together. Default 50M.
PP_MAX_PUBLICATION_BYTES=50M

# ── Storage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Relative to the working directory, so run the server from apps/server or this
# moves. The `worker` profile bind-mounts this exact path.
PP_BLOB_ROOT=./data/blobs

PP_BLOB_BACKEND=local
# With `--profile s3` (SeaweedFS from compose.dev.yml). The worker must use the
# same backend, so mirror PP_BLOB_BACKEND into deploy/compose/.env; its
# endpoint differs (PP_S3_ENDPOINT_INTERNAL=http://seaweedfs:8333):
# PP_BLOB_BACKEND=s3
# PP_S3_BUCKET=pphub
# PP_S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8333
# PP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=pphub
# PP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=pphub-dev-secret
# PP_S3_PATH_STYLE=1

# ── Development ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fixed development session key. NEVER in production — but it must be set here
# if you want office thumbnails, since the worker container needs to derive the
# same key to sign conversion tokens this server verifies.
PP_DEV_INSECURE=1

# Production instead: openssl rand -base64 32
# PP_SESSION_KEY=

# ── Outgoing mail (SMTP) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional fallback; the admin console can set or override it.
# PP_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# PP_SMTP_PORT=587
# PP_SMTP_USERNAME=
# PP_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# PP_SMTP_FROM=pp-hub <noreply@example.com>
# PP_SMTP_TLS=starttls

# ── Observability ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PP_LOG_LEVEL=info       # debug | info | warn | error
# PP_LOG_FORMAT=text      # text | json
# PP_METRICS_ADDR=:9091   # Prometheus /metrics; `off` disables it
